<article class="env-corollary" id="005CCE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/005CCE">Corollary <span data-tag="005CCE">6.2.3.11</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be a semitopos, and let $\{  f_{\alpha }: X_{\alpha } \rightarrow Y_{\alpha } \} $ be a (small) collection of effective epimorphisms in $\calX $. Then the induced map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f: \coprod _{\alpha } X_{\alpha } \rightarrow \coprod _{\alpha } Y_{\alpha }  \]
</div>
  <p> is an effective epimorphism. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Proposition <a href="/tag/5C64D1" data-tag="5C64D1">6.2.3.10</a> with Remark <a href="/tag/1477B3" data-tag="1477B3">6.2.3.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>